CREATED:20260814T134718Z
DESCRIPTION:All Hallows' Eve service is a festival in the church that reca
 lls the faith and witness of those who have carried on and cherished the 
 Christian faith throughout history. The service celebrates the Church's c
 ontinuing communion with these men and women and memorializes the recentl
 y deceased. It comprises scripture readings\, testimonies about saints\, 
 and anthems. The name of the service comes from its celebration on the ni
 ght before All Saints' (or All Hallows') so it's "All Hallows' Eve\," or 
 "Halloween" (Halloween costumes are welcome at this service!).\n\nAll are
  welcome at this service. Free parking is available in the Bryan Center G
 arage at 125 Science Drive. ADA parking is available in the surface lot a
 t the same address.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261021T181726Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261031T223000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T181726Z
