DESCRIPTION:The Sperling Center for Jewish Studies invites students\, facu
 lty\, and community members to attend the 2026 Jewish Studies Annual Rese
 arch Symposium on Sunday\, November 1\, 2026. This annual event showcases
  innovative research by Duke undergraduate and graduate students\, as wel
 l as affiliated fellows\, whose work engages Jewish history\, culture\, r
 eligion\, literature\, politics\, and society across diverse geographical
  and historical contexts.\n\nThe symposium provides an opportunity for em
 erging scholars to present original research\, share recent findings\, an
 d engage in interdisciplinary conversations with faculty\, students\, and
  members of the broader community. Presentations highlight the breadth of
  scholarship taking place across Duke and demonstrate the vibrant intelle
 ctual life fostered by the Center for Jewish Studies.\n\nThe symposium is
  free and open to the public. More information\, including a detailed sch
 edule and speaker bios\, can be found at: https://jewishstudies.duke.edu/
 2026-sperling-center-jewish-studies-research-symposium
DURATION:PT5H
