CREATED:20260616T143517Z
DESCRIPTION:Praised by The Washington Post as "one of this country's most 
 interesting and profound pianists" Awadagin Pratt is one of the most dist
 inctive artists in American classical music. Winner of the Naumburg Inter
 national Piano Competition and recipient of an Avery Fisher Career Grant\
 , Pratt has built a dynamic career with appearances ranging from solo rec
 itals at Carnegie Hall and the Kennedy Center to collaborations with lead
 ing orchestras across the country. \n\nHis program\, America 250\, reflec
 ts on the breadth of American musical voices. Works by Florence Price\, G
 eorge Walker\, and Nathaniel Dett appear alongside music by contemporary 
 composers including Judd Greenstein and Fred Hersch. Pratt also performs 
 his own arrangement of the spiritual Sometimes I Feel Like a Motherless C
 hild\, before closing with Brahms' monumental Variations and Fugue on a T
 heme of Handel.
DURATION:PT1H40M
