CREATED:20260928T181646Z
DESCRIPTION:5PM reception with DJ GrayGray from House Music for ALS\n6PM F
 ilm Screening and Q&A with Dr. Richard Bedlack\n\nREGISTER TO ATTEND!\n\n
 Stitching Strength is a documentary film that captures the fight against 
 ALS - a terminal disease that strips away the body's control - through le
 ns of creativity\, courage\, and connection.\n\nAt its heart is Dr. Richa
 rd Bedlack\, a neurologist whose bold fashion and bolder optimism set the
  tone for a radically different kind of care. But this isn't just his sto
 ry. It's about the patients who refuse to be defined by their diagnosis\,
  and the families who turn grief into art\, music\, and action.\n\nThis i
 s not a story of surrender. It's a story of style\, strength\, and the po
 wer of believing in what's still possible. For Dr. Bedlack\, fashion isn'
 t just how you dress - it's an expression of joy. A conversation starter.
  A shield against despair. It's medicine. Clothing becomes a way for pati
 ents to reclaim their identity\, adorn themselves with dignity\, and expr
 ess the parts of themselves ALS can't touch. Style becomes a tool for hea
 ling\, not just expression. From accessible runway designs to custom suit
 s lined with symbolism\, every stitch is an act of strength. Read more ab
 out Stitching Strength.\n\nOpening reception will feature DJ GrayGray fro
 m House Music for ALS.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260928T181646Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261102T170000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T181646Z
